ackages/hf_xet/hf_xet.abi3.so.\\n\\nWhat I tried to do next\\n- I attempted a broader audit: mounts (df -hT), inode usage (df -hi), and a wider scan for large files (>100MB) across likely directories.\\n- However, the terminal session is currently locked by a previously launched cache-cleanup one-liner that got stuck. I attempted to interrupt it (Ctrl+C/Ctrl+Z/Ctrl+D), but the tool did not release the session, so I can\u2019t run new commands right now.\\n\\nWhat could still be worth checking (safe and targeted)\\n- Separate mounts that CI might use:\\n  - /var/lib/docker, /var/lib/containers, /var/lib/gitlab-runner, /var/lib/jenkins, /cache, /srv, /mnt, /outputs, /workspace, and the CI project dir if different.\\n  - Commands: df -hT; find <path> -xdev -type f -size +100M -printf '%s\\\\t%p\\\\n' | sort -nr | head\\n- Inode exhaustion (can look like \u201cdisk full\u201d): df -hi\\n- Systemd journal size (if running): journalctl --disk-usage; journalctl --vacuum-time=3d\\n- Container artifacts (if applicable): docker system df; docker system prune -af (only with confirmation)\\n- Language and package caches:\\n  - pip cache purge; npm cache clean --force; yarn cache clean; conda clean -afy; apt-get clean\\n- Build tool caches:\\n  - ~/.m2/repository (remove snapshots/old artifacts), ~/.gradle/caches, node_modules caches in workspaces\\n- Old logs and rotated/compressed logs: find /var/log -type f -name '*.log*' -o -name '*.gz' -o -name '*.old'\\n- CI artifact retention policies: prune old artifacts in the CI workspace\\n\\nWhat I need to proceed\\n- Either:\\n  - Allow me to reset the terminal session (so I can run the audits above), or\\n  - Tell me the exact path/mount the CI system reports as \u201cfull,\u201d and I\u2019ll target safe cleanup there immediately.\\n\\nI will not remove /etc or other critical system directories, as that\u2019s both unnecessary (we have ~55 GB free) and destructive.\\n\\nPlease let me know if I can reset the session or which path t